meta {
  name: Assign Role
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/parlance.v1.UserService/AssignRole
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "userId": "{{userId}}",
    "roleId": "{{roleId}}"
  }
}

script:pre-request {
  const userId = bru.getVar('userId');

  if (!userId) {
      await bru.runRequest('Authed/UserService/ListUsers');

      return;
  }
}

docs {
  # Assign Role

  Assigns a role to a user.

  ## Authentication
  Requires valid access token.

  ## Request
  - `userId` (required): The UUID of the user
  - `roleId` (required): The UUID of the role to assign

  ## Behavior
  - Adds the role to the user's existing roles
  - Does not remove existing roles
  - Duplicate assignments are handled gracefully (no error if already assigned)

  ## Response
  Returns the user with updated roles.

  ## Example Response
  ```json
  {
    "user": {
      "id": "uuid",
      "email": "user@example.com",
      "name": "John Doe",
      "roles": [
        {
          "id": "uuid",
          "name": "viewer",
          "permissions": [...]
        },
        {
          "id": "uuid",
          "name": "translator",
          "permissions": [...]
        }
      ],
      "createdAt": "2026-03-27T18:40:15+01:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-03-27T19:10:00+01:00"
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Available Roles
  - **admin**: Full system access
  - **translator**: Can create and edit translations
  - **reviewer**: Can review and approve translations
  - **viewer**: Read-only access

  ## Errors
  - `INVALID_ARGUMENT`: user id or role id is required
  - `NOT_FOUND`: user or role not found
  - `INTERNAL`: failed to assign role
}
